the exynos framebuffer driver did not supply an implementation of fb_imageblit,
leading to an instant crash when fbcon invokes it without checking.
genric implementations of framebuffer operations are available via:
CONFIG_FB_CFB_FILLRECT, CONFIG_FB_CFB_COPYAREA, CONFIG_FB_CFB_IMAGEBLIT=y
but were not wired up in the driver.
(also wires up cfb_copyarea, have not tested if it's needed.)

--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu_9810/decon_core.c.old      2026-09-22 17:34:26.914671726 +0000
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu_9810/decon_core.c  2026-09-22 17:34:53.277294075 +0000
@@ -3033,6 +3033,8 @@
        .fb_blank       = decon_blank,
        .fb_setcolreg   = decon_setcolreg,
+       .fb_copyarea    = cfb_copyarea,
        .fb_fillrect    = cfb_fillrect,
+       .fb_imageblit   = cfb_imageblit,
 #ifdef CONFIG_COMPAT
        .fb_compat_ioctl = decon_compat_ioctl,
 #endif
